From ddd526411547d51b719422e8a7add90a365d6bb8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 21:00:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] gps: expose GNSS debug data and non-framework location
 notifications

Implements the two nyx GPS methods added alongside this: get_debug_data and
set_nfw_callback.

get_debug_data fetches IGnssDebug::getDebugData and renders it as text - the
engine's position and time estimates, and per-satellite ephemeris state. That
is the question to ask when a device streams NMEA at 1Hz but never reports a
satellite in view, which is where both test devices currently sit. The
satellite array is a hidl_vec whose element layout depends on enum widths the
HAL does not pin down, so a mismatch makes the vec read fail rather than
misparse, and the position and time are still reported in that case.

set_nfw_callback registers with IGnssVisibilityControl, which lives in its own
package - android.hardware.gnss.visibility_control - and exists only from @2.0,
being the model that replaced the NI interface @2.0 retires. Its callback needs
care the others did not: isInEmergencySession generates a value, so it must be
answered or the HAL blocks. We answer false, because nothing plumbs emergency
call state into this module and claiming an emergency session is exactly the
claim that bypasses the user's consent. NfwNotification's three hidl_strings
are read from the parcel after the struct, in field order, as the NI
notification's are.

Both are addressed with @1.0 descriptors where the method is @1.0-declared -
getDebugData is inherited by @2.0::IGnssDebug - following the rule that cost us
IAGnssRil earlier.

Upstream-Status: Pending
